  recipeId: resistor
  concept: 'Authored objective: R1 Series Resistor Conducting.

    Authored requirement:
    Fixed 220 ohm series resistor R1 must conduct. Connection pair Resistor_220_Input
    and Resistor_220_Output. Conduction required.

    General teaching principle:
    Resistance, voltage and current are linked by Ohm''s law for ideal resistors,
    while power dissipation needs separate evaluation.

    Only fresh, authoritative
    game evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A flow restriction can suggest resistance; unlike a pipe, a resistor follows
    electrical laws.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Current and resistor power cannot be established without voltage/current
    evidence and component values.
